Subject: CEB Slice 05 Neural Routing

& [WorkSlice] is the evidence-gated learned candidate-routing boundary
  + [slice_uuid] is 9ca04f5a-dc87-46f2-8045-14fa8e6c0498
  + [status] is specification_only_and_adoption_blocked
  + [depends_on] is stable semantic fabric, deterministic query baseline, reviewed corpus, metrics, failure thresholds, and fallback proof
  + [requirement_set] is CEB-016, CEB-017, CEB-018, CEB-019, and CEB-020
  + [deliverable] is optional digest-bound candidate router evaluated first in shadow mode
  + [excluded] is semantic authority, signature authority, source resolution, proof generation, and mandatory-gate bypass

& [SupportRecord] is a deliberate gap record
  + [specification_support] is Cantor Neural-Routed Gated Semantic Fabric and canonical build specification
  + [baseline_support] is absent
  + [corpus_support] is absent
  + [implementation_support] is absent
  + [test_support] is adoption gate defined but not executable
  + [proof_support] is absent
  + [gap] is model family and acceptance threshold must be chosen from deterministic evidence, not architectural preference

& [ActivationGate] is mandatory
  = must: preserve provenance for every reviewed routing example
  = must: bind router artifact to fabric, address, relation, corpus, and model digests
  = must: compare against deterministic retrieval in shadow mode
  = must: prove material gain and acceptable regressions
  = must: prove zero authority-gate bypass and deterministic fallback
  - never: implement or call the router production-ready before every gate passes
